  ["tojson"] = {
    children = {},
    description = [[
Converts a Lus value to JSON. A table whose complete key set is the contiguous integer range from 1 through `n` becomes an array. Other tables become objects that retain string keys and omit keys of other types. The empty table becomes `[]`. JSON object member order is unspecified.

The optional `filter` is called first with `nil, value` for the root, then with integer array keys or string object keys. Its returned value is serialized recursively, and returning `nil` omits a field or produces `null` at the root. A table's `__json` metamethod can return any serializable replacement value.

Bigints and decimals serialize with their exact digits. Non-finite numbers become `null`. Functions, threads, userdata, vectors, and enum values become `null` at the root or in arrays and are omitted from objects. Shared acyclic tables are serialized by value. Cycles raise errors. Serialization enforces a 1,000-level nesting ceiling and follows the interpreter's C-call limit, which can raise a C stack overflow first for deeply nested tables.]],
    kind = "function",
    module = "base",
    name = "tojson",
    origin = "lus",
    params = {
      {
        name = "value",
        type = "any",
      },
      {
        name = "filter",
        optional = true,
        type = "function",
      },
    },
    parent = nil,
    returns = {
      {
        type = "string",
      },
    },
    short_name = "tojson",
    since = "0.1.0",
    source = "stdlib/base/tojson.md",
    stability = "stable",
  },
  ["tonumber"] = {
    children = {},
    description = [[
Converts `e` to a number. Integers and floats are returned unchanged. A bigint or a decimal converts to the nearest float, which makes `tonumber` the explicit way to mix an exact number with float arithmetic. If `e` is a string, tries to parse it as a numeral, and a numeral that overflows 64 bits becomes a float. If `e` is an enum value, returns its 1-based index. The optional `base` accepts an integer from 2 through 36 and specifies the base for string conversion, in which case `e` must be a string. Returns `nil` on failure.

The functions `bigint` and `decimal` convert strings to exact numbers.]],
    fastcall = true,
    kind = "function",
    module = "base",
    name = "tonumber",
    origin = "lua",
    params = {
      {
        name = "e",
        type = "any",
